\subsection{Temporal Smoothing \& Cumulative AF Burden Agreement}
As shown in Table~\ref{tab:hmm} and Figure~\ref{fig:burden}, raw window-level aggregation across the 98 annotated Holters exhibited high variance. Moving average temporal smoothing (9 windows, 270s) achieved strong concordance with cardiologist ground truth ($r = \mathbf{0.7236}$, Spearman $\rho = \mathbf{0.7909}$) and reduced cumulative burden Mean Absolute Error by \textbf{50.1\%} from 30.64\% down to \textbf{15.30\% points}.

